WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.367 --> 00:00:02.835
-Our first guest tonight
is an Emmy-nominated actor

00:00:02.835 --> 00:00:05.471
you know from his work on shows
such as "Justified," "Deadwood,"

00:00:05.471 --> 00:00:06.806
and "Santa Clarita Diet."

00:00:06.806 --> 00:00:08.474
You can see him next
in "Amsterdam,"

00:00:08.474 --> 00:00:10.777
which premieres in theaters
October 7th.

00:00:10.777 --> 00:00:11.911
Let's take a look.

00:00:11.911 --> 00:00:14.513
-Then I saw the man,
this red-faced man,

00:00:14.513 --> 00:00:16.149
the man who pushed Liz Meekins.

00:00:16.149 --> 00:00:17.983
And he looked right at me
and he said...

00:00:17.983 --> 00:00:20.687
-This is your moment
to end your inferiority.

00:00:20.687 --> 00:00:22.422
You can have that procedure.

00:00:22.422 --> 00:00:27.560 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:28.694
-Don't move!

00:00:28.694 --> 00:00:30.696
-[ Grunting ]

00:00:30.696 --> 00:00:31.664
[ Gun clicks ]

00:00:31.664 --> 00:00:33.066
-[Bleep]

00:00:33.066 --> 00:00:34.767
[ Gunshot ]

00:00:34.767 --> 00:00:37.937
-[ Grunting ]

00:00:37.937 --> 00:00:39.272
-Come on.
-Stop those people.

00:00:39.272 --> 00:00:40.506
-Please welcome back to the show

00:00:40.506 --> 00:00:42.675
my very good friend
Timothy Olyphant!

00:00:42.675 --> 00:00:44.811
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:44.811 --> 00:00:54.287 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:54.287 --> 00:01:03.796 line:0%
♪♪

00:01:03.796 --> 00:01:13.272 line:0%
♪♪

00:01:13.272 --> 00:01:14.641
-Please sit down.
-I want -- I feel --

00:01:14.641 --> 00:01:17.743
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Thank you. Huh?

00:01:17.743 --> 00:01:19.678
-I want you -- I want you
to admit to them

00:01:19.678 --> 00:01:20.813
what you just told me.

00:01:20.813 --> 00:01:23.116
-No, no, this is your show.
That's your job.

00:01:23.116 --> 00:01:24.484
Let me tell you something --

00:01:24.484 --> 00:01:26.352
-Alright, well, can I tell them
what you just told me?

00:01:26.352 --> 00:01:28.087
-Please, go for it.
-You -- We shook hands.

00:01:28.087 --> 00:01:29.222
I said, "Thanks for being here."

00:01:29.222 --> 00:01:30.823
And then you --
you wouldn't let go.

00:01:30.823 --> 00:01:33.025
-Uh-huh.
-And you said, "I told my wife

00:01:33.025 --> 00:01:35.562
I'm gonna hold this hug
for an uncomfortably long time."

00:01:35.562 --> 00:01:37.463
[ Laughter ]

00:01:37.463 --> 00:01:39.732
-Yeah.
And then she said --

00:01:39.732 --> 00:01:41.901
I said, "Because the audience
likes that.

00:01:41.901 --> 00:01:43.436
They -- They think we're
talking about something."

00:01:43.436 --> 00:01:45.304
-Yeah.
-And she said -- And she said,

00:01:45.304 --> 00:01:46.639
"Tim, you're trying too hard."

00:01:46.639 --> 00:01:48.174
[ Laughter ]

00:01:48.174 --> 00:01:50.510
-You told me that whole exchange
while we were over there, yeah.

00:01:50.510 --> 00:01:52.178
-That's -- That's what happened.

00:01:52.178 --> 00:01:54.046
-This is very nice --
-And I gotta say.

00:01:54.046 --> 00:01:55.381
-What?
-I think I was trying too hard.

00:01:55.381 --> 00:01:56.682
-You do?
-Yeah, yeah.

00:01:56.682 --> 00:01:58.284
No, I think she's right.
I think I was trying too hard.

00:01:58.284 --> 00:02:00.553
You guys are going for it
right now.

00:02:00.553 --> 00:02:04.156
But I also think she was right.
-You know what?

00:02:04.156 --> 00:02:06.292
I like that you held me
for a really long time

00:02:06.292 --> 00:02:07.727
and then you still
made a real meal,

00:02:07.727 --> 00:02:09.862
like, making a real long loop.

00:02:09.862 --> 00:02:11.730
Did the --
You pointed at the band.

00:02:11.730 --> 00:02:13.700
-Honestly, I got a little lost.

00:02:13.700 --> 00:02:15.934
Because it's been a while.
-It has been a while.

00:02:15.934 --> 00:02:18.037
-It's been a long time since --
since I've seen you.

00:02:18.037 --> 00:02:19.606
It's lovely to see you,
by the way.

00:02:19.606 --> 00:02:21.974
And lovely to see all of you
and the band.

00:02:21.974 --> 00:02:24.810
I appreciate the band.
I see Syd there.

00:02:24.810 --> 00:02:26.145
What?
-All of your --

00:02:26.145 --> 00:02:27.713
All of your appearances
on this show were memorable,

00:02:27.713 --> 00:02:29.782
but we had
a very memorable Zoom.

00:02:29.782 --> 00:02:33.218
Uh, and sort of
sartorially memorable

00:02:33.218 --> 00:02:34.553
because of what
you were wearing.

00:02:34.553 --> 00:02:36.088
Uh, a very charming hat,

00:02:36.088 --> 00:02:37.590
and then the whole interview
I'm like,

00:02:37.590 --> 00:02:40.192
"Is that a Van Halen jersey?"

00:02:40.192 --> 00:02:41.361
What is that?

00:02:41.361 --> 00:02:43.462
-Yeah, no, I picked it up
at one of the shows.

00:02:43.462 --> 00:02:44.564
That's a Van Halen jersey.

00:02:44.564 --> 00:02:46.098
-Okay, so you went
to a Van Halen show,

00:02:46.098 --> 00:02:47.400
and you bought -- that's merch?

00:02:47.400 --> 00:02:48.734
-Yeah.

00:02:48.734 --> 00:02:51.271
Which is big for me
that I bought something.

00:02:51.271 --> 00:02:53.539
'Cause I'm pretty -- I'm into
the -- I'm in show business.

00:02:53.539 --> 00:02:55.474
-Yeah.
-I like the free stuff.

00:02:55.474 --> 00:02:59.979
But -- But I paid for that
at a Van Halen show.

00:02:59.979 --> 00:03:01.113
It was a good show,

00:03:01.113 --> 00:03:03.282
and Eddie had passed away,
perhaps that day.

00:03:03.282 --> 00:03:06.152
-Rest in peace, yeah.
-And so I broke out the shirt.

00:03:06.152 --> 00:03:08.621
It was the day -- It was
in honor of Eddie Van Halen.

00:03:08.621 --> 00:03:09.956
-You know, there's
another interesting thing

00:03:09.956 --> 00:03:12.224
about show business,
where some people will --

00:03:12.224 --> 00:03:13.425
you know,
they'll get a stylist,

00:03:13.425 --> 00:03:15.394
and they'll wear
a piece of clothing once.

00:03:15.394 --> 00:03:17.230
-Yeah, it's been
recommended to me.

00:03:17.230 --> 00:03:18.364
[ Laughter ]

00:03:18.364 --> 00:03:19.899
-But we noticed something
about your hat.

00:03:19.899 --> 00:03:22.167
You just had the premiere
for your film "Amsterdam,"

00:03:22.167 --> 00:03:24.203
and, uh, I think
you double dipped.

00:03:24.203 --> 00:03:25.371
-Yeah.

00:03:25.371 --> 00:03:26.639
-So the hat --
-Yeah.

00:03:26.639 --> 00:03:30.209
-The hat's back.
-Yeah.

00:03:30.209 --> 00:03:32.879
I was terribly underdressed.
I have to admit.

00:03:32.879 --> 00:03:34.947
-No, don't -- don't say
you're terribly underdressed.

00:03:34.947 --> 00:03:36.749
Here's Drake at the same thing.

00:03:36.749 --> 00:03:39.018
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:39.018 --> 00:03:41.453
-He might have overdid it,
but --

00:03:41.453 --> 00:03:44.523
It doesn't appear
as though the invitation

00:03:44.523 --> 00:03:45.691
just said "dress code."

00:03:45.691 --> 00:03:47.226
It said, "Your call."
-Yeah.

00:03:47.226 --> 00:03:49.962
-Whatever you want.
Because, yeah, I -- yeah.

00:03:49.962 --> 00:03:51.764
-It does feel like
you just realized

00:03:51.764 --> 00:03:53.532
what your cast members
are wearing,

00:03:53.532 --> 00:03:56.135
and you look like you're about
to, like, make a break for it.

00:03:56.135 --> 00:03:58.938
You have -- You have the gait
of a man who's about to leave.

00:03:58.938 --> 00:04:01.006
-I will say, before I forget,

00:04:01.006 --> 00:04:02.675
because I often do forget
to say this,

00:04:02.675 --> 00:04:06.245
it was just a genuine pleasure
to be part of that film.

00:04:06.245 --> 00:04:07.480
-Yeah, and a wonderful cast.

00:04:07.480 --> 00:04:09.581
-It meant a great deal
to be part of that film.

00:04:09.581 --> 00:04:11.985
And every step along the way
has just been --

00:04:11.985 --> 00:04:13.653
-And they tried real hard
in the clip --

00:04:13.653 --> 00:04:15.120
they tried real hard
to give you ugly face.

00:04:15.120 --> 00:04:16.289
Still can't do it.
-It was clear --

00:04:16.289 --> 00:04:18.825
It did occur to me
when I showed up on set

00:04:18.825 --> 00:04:20.192
and I'd gone through
hair and makeup

00:04:20.192 --> 00:04:22.528
that he clearly had somebody
else in mind for the part.

00:04:22.528 --> 00:04:24.597
[ Laughter ]

00:04:24.597 --> 00:04:26.332
But -- 'Cause I said to him --

00:04:26.332 --> 00:04:28.067
It's a David O. Russell film,

00:04:28.067 --> 00:04:30.269
one of my favorite filmmakers
of all time.

00:04:30.269 --> 00:04:33.539
And at one point,
I do remember saying to him,

00:04:33.539 --> 00:04:35.974
"You know, you probably
could have just hired someone

00:04:35.974 --> 00:04:37.143
who looked like this."

00:04:37.143 --> 00:04:38.844
[ Laughter ]

00:04:38.844 --> 00:04:40.713
"I mean,
I'm thrilled to be here.

00:04:40.713 --> 00:04:42.114
I'm glad you didn't."
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:04:42.114 --> 00:04:44.450
-It was really
quite a thrilling experience.

00:04:44.450 --> 00:04:46.251
-Do you --
We've talked about your kids.

00:04:46.251 --> 00:04:47.687
You've got three --
two girls and a boy.

00:04:47.687 --> 00:04:50.422
Do they give you feedback when
you show up in public like this?

00:04:50.422 --> 00:04:53.225
Or is that -- is that a thing
where you don't hear much?

00:04:53.225 --> 00:04:56.796
-Uh, well, I -- They weren't --
I didn't bring this up.

00:04:56.796 --> 00:04:59.465
So my --
They don't give a [bleep]

00:04:59.465 --> 00:05:01.066
-They don't give a [bleep]
-Yeah.

00:05:01.066 --> 00:05:03.736
-But you -- I should note, one
of your co-stars, Taylor Swift.

00:05:03.736 --> 00:05:04.770
-Yeah.
-Did they --

00:05:04.770 --> 00:05:06.605
-No.
-That matters, right?

00:05:06.605 --> 00:05:09.775
-Yeah.
Yeah, my kids have gotten --

00:05:09.775 --> 00:05:12.244
They get very excited
about people in the --

00:05:12.244 --> 00:05:14.747
Music business people,
they get very excited.

00:05:14.747 --> 00:05:16.949
Taylor they were
very excited about.

00:05:16.949 --> 00:05:18.984
Yeah, and I'm aware of it,
so I'll tell them,

00:05:18.984 --> 00:05:20.719
"Yeah, I'm working
with Taylor Swift today."

00:05:20.719 --> 00:05:23.589
Because, you know,
you try to get a little --

00:05:23.589 --> 00:05:24.990
-A little currency
with the kids?

00:05:24.990 --> 00:05:26.892
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:26.892 --> 00:05:29.528
Listen, you're gonna --
you're gonna --

00:05:29.528 --> 00:05:31.797
You don't know this yet, but
you're gonna get to this place,

00:05:31.797 --> 00:05:35.101
and it feels like desperation,
where you're like --

00:05:35.101 --> 00:05:37.903
You catch yourself saying, like,

00:05:37.903 --> 00:05:40.840
"I'm working
with Taylor Swift today."

00:05:40.840 --> 00:05:42.675
And as soon as you say it,
you're like,

00:05:42.675 --> 00:05:44.911
"What the [bleep]
is wrong with me?

00:05:44.911 --> 00:05:49.182
Why am I trying to impress
my own goddamn children?"

00:05:49.182 --> 00:05:50.350
They're my --
You know what I mean?

00:05:50.350 --> 00:05:51.650
-And they can smell it on you,
right?

00:05:51.650 --> 00:05:54.386
-Oh, my God, they can smell it.

00:05:54.386 --> 00:05:57.522
But I know they're --
That is the only thing.

00:05:57.522 --> 00:06:00.459
You know, I was at --

00:06:00.459 --> 00:06:02.428
The greatest thing
that ever happened to me,

00:06:02.428 --> 00:06:03.695
as far as my children
are concerned.

00:06:03.695 --> 00:06:09.068
We were at the "Once Upon a Time
in Hollywood" --

00:06:09.068 --> 00:06:10.303
What was that film called?
-Yeah, yeah.

00:06:10.303 --> 00:06:11.404
The Quentin Tarantino film?

00:06:11.404 --> 00:06:12.572
-"Once Upon a Time
in Hollywood."

00:06:12.572 --> 00:06:14.306
-Yeah.
DiCaprio, Brad Pitt.

00:06:14.306 --> 00:06:16.508
-Exactly.
So, we're at that premiere.

00:06:16.508 --> 00:06:17.844
And my kids, for the most part,

00:06:17.844 --> 00:06:19.144
we never took them
to any of these things.

00:06:19.144 --> 00:06:21.847
But now they're older.
They're out of the house.

00:06:21.847 --> 00:06:24.817
We miss 'em.
-Yeah.

00:06:24.817 --> 00:06:26.852
[ Laughter ]

00:06:26.852 --> 00:06:28.454
-It's so nice.

00:06:28.454 --> 00:06:29.521
[ Laughter ]

00:06:29.521 --> 00:06:31.857
So nice.

00:06:31.857 --> 00:06:34.493
We miss 'em, but, oh, my God.

00:06:34.493 --> 00:06:35.961
Anyway, we take 'em
to the premiere,

00:06:35.961 --> 00:06:39.198
and that's when it --

00:06:39.198 --> 00:06:42.901
Brad Pitt and then Leo,
and it was all very exciting,

00:06:42.901 --> 00:06:44.503
but when they saw Snoop Dogg...

00:06:44.503 --> 00:06:46.005
-Really?
-Oh, my God.

00:06:46.005 --> 00:06:47.373
-That was the one?

00:06:47.373 --> 00:06:49.508
-Like, they were like,
"Oh, my God, it's --"

00:06:49.508 --> 00:06:51.276
They went crazy.

00:06:51.276 --> 00:06:54.546
They went crazy.
They were so excited.

00:06:54.546 --> 00:06:58.584
And we were with someone
who knew him,

00:06:58.584 --> 00:06:59.785
and said, "Do you want
to come meet him?"

00:06:59.785 --> 00:07:01.554
And they were like,
"Of course we do.

00:07:01.554 --> 00:07:03.956
Of course we do."
They were so excited.

00:07:03.956 --> 00:07:05.691
And it was the greatest thing
that ever could happen to me

00:07:05.691 --> 00:07:07.159
in front of my kids.

00:07:07.159 --> 00:07:10.763
When I was first -- I was the
first to be introduced to him,

00:07:10.763 --> 00:07:13.565
and he looked at me.

00:07:13.565 --> 00:07:16.135
You know, someone said,
"Snoop, Tim. Tim, Snoop."

00:07:16.135 --> 00:07:19.672
And he looked at me and goes,
"You're a bad mother[bleep]"

00:07:19.672 --> 00:07:21.207
[ Laughter ]

00:07:21.207 --> 00:07:23.309
-That's the best.
That's the best.

00:07:23.309 --> 00:07:25.044
I mean...

00:07:25.044 --> 00:07:27.012
-I tried so hard --

00:07:27.012 --> 00:07:28.814
You don't understand
what it took for me

00:07:28.814 --> 00:07:31.016
to stay focused and cool...
-Yeah.

00:07:31.016 --> 00:07:35.254
-...in that moment and not
look at my children and go...

00:07:35.254 --> 00:07:38.023
[ Laughter ]

00:07:38.023 --> 00:07:40.426
Like, the most uncool thing.
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:07:40.426 --> 00:07:41.793
So you just had to take it.

00:07:41.793 --> 00:07:44.363
-I literally almost looked
at them and said, "See!"

00:07:44.363 --> 00:07:46.098
[ Laughter ]

00:07:46.098 --> 00:07:48.100
"Do you not see?"

00:07:48.100 --> 00:07:49.568
-Alright, well,
you gotta stick around,

00:07:49.568 --> 00:07:51.403
'cause I have a lot more
questions about your kids.

00:07:51.403 --> 00:07:52.405
We'll be right back.

